00\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00f6\u00ff\u00a9\u0000\u00ab\u0001Fast, agile and just entering production, the NeoTech NWM-1N is the first mech produced by NeoTech, Inc, a Clan Wolf in Exile c"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 783,
      "end": 1083,
      "text": "ompany.\r\n\r\nThe NeoWolf is designed as a multi-role mech.  With the Active Probe and the TAG unit, it can seek out shutdown mechs and equipment and call down a rain of fire upon them.   The ER-PPC gives it Sniper ability, while the claw and the Medium Pulse Laser allow it to get close and brawl.   \r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 1083,
      "end": 1760,
      "length": 675,
      "text": "This NeoWolf Variant is a platform of high technology.  Though it does have an LRM 10 pack mounted, it is a streak pack, a touch of experimental technology that has good reliability for such new technology.  However, it's really close hitting power is given by the 2 Heavy Medium Lasers and thier ER Medium Laser cousin.  Again, it's jack of all trades status shows as this is not a pitch down, brawl it out configuration.  It's close saving grace is the claw, which is still apparent in this configuration, forcing anyone who gets close to suffer badly from it.\r\nNote that this configuration also drops the BAP and the ECM suite, spending more space towards the weapondry.\r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 1760,
      "end": 1906,
      "length": 144,
      "text": "No battle history so far for this mech.  Trials are doing well with the Wolves in Exile and the FC.  Primarily used as a sniper with both groups"
    },
